 Workarounds
 ===========
 
+KK_WORKAROUND_18
+----------------
+| macOS version: 27.0
+| Metal ticket: Not reported
+| Metal ticket status:
+| CTS test failure: ``dEQP-VK.api.copy_and_blit.core.use_after_copy.*.transfer_dst_optimal.1024x1024x2*_color_att_flag_img2img``
+| Comments:
+
+A render command encoder that already ran one draw drops most of the
+primitives of a later draw that writes a different ``render_target_array_index``.
+The layer the first draw wrote stays correct, the newly selected layer keeps
+whatever the attachment held before the pass, and the primitives are dropped
+rather than routed to the wrong layer: the previously written layer is never
+disturbed.
+
+The loss is deterministic, and only the trailing part of the second draw
+survives. A layered pass drawing 1048576 points per layer into a
+1024x1024x2 ``R32G32B32A32_SFLOAT`` attachment loses exactly the first 908672
+points of the second draw on the first such pass in a fresh process; later
+passes in the same process are correct. Triangles behave the same way, losing
+933472 of 1048576 covered texels. Three or four layers lose the same amount on
+every layer after the first.
+
+A ``VK_ATTACHMENT_LOAD_OP_CLEAR`` load op on the same pass renders correctly,
+while ``LOAD`` and ``DONT_CARE`` both lose the primitives, so only a pass that
+does not clear its attachments is affected. That is not used to narrow the
+workaround, because it rests on a single configuration and three earlier
+narrowings of this failure were each refuted by the next measurement.
+
+``inputPrimitiveTopology`` is already set from the pipeline's topology class,
+``renderTargetArrayLength`` is already the attachment layer count, and the MSL
+vertex output already declares ``[[render_target_array_index]]``, so none of
+the documented requirements for layered rendering are unmet. Neither an
+encoder-scope nor a queue-scope barrier between the draws helps, and neither
+does dropping the single-view ``setVertexAmplificationCount`` call or clearing
+``allowGPUOptimizedContents``. Only ending the render command encoder and
+starting a new one restores the dropped primitives.
+
+Splitting the draws into smaller ones does not avoid the loss either: 1048576
+points issued as four draws of 262144 still lose 653984 of them, so there is no
+primitive count below which a later draw is safe and the workaround cannot be
+gated on a draw size.
+
+The workaround therefore restarts the render command encoder before any Metal
+draw that is not the first in the current encoder, whenever the pass is layered
+and the stage that feeds the rasterizer writes the layer: the emulated geometry
+shader's raster draw, else the tessellation evaluation shader, else the vertex
+shader. Each entry of a multi-draw is a Metal draw of its own, so every entry
+after the first restarts the encoder as a separate draw call would. Restarting reuses the existing
+render-pass flush path, so the attachments are reloaded and nothing is lost.
+The cost is one attachment load and store per such draw; a pass that never
+writes the layer, or is not layered, is untouched. The
+``kosmickrisp_layered_draw_sequence`` test reproduces the loss without the
+workaround, and ``kosmickrisp_layered_draw_multi_draw`` and
+``kosmickrisp_layered_draw_geometry`` reproduce it through a multi-draw and
+through a geometry shader's layer: without the per-draw restart and the
+raster-stage check, each loses the same 908672 points.
+
+Restarting an encoder mid-pass has to preserve everything the open encoder
+was carrying. Vertex amplification was the one piece that did not survive:
+``vkCmdClearAttachments`` turns amplification off because the meta clear
+routes its own layers, and the restart used to hand the meta draw the pass's
+multiview mapping again, so in a multiview pass the clear landed on the wrong
+layers - ``dEQP-VK.multiview.dynamic_rendering.clear_attachments.no_queries``
+``.5_10_5_10`` put view mask 10's clear on layers 0 and 2. The amplification
+mapping is therefore recorded in the graphics state and replayed by every
+encoder start, and ``kosmickrisp_multiview_clear_attachments`` covers it.
+
+| Log:
+| 2026-09-12: Workaround implemented
+
